WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.052
The standard way to import NumPy is with the short name N P.

00:00:06.052 --> 00:00:09.857
In the code, you will see import NumPy as N P.

00:00:09.857 --> 00:00:16.711
After that, we can use the NumPy array function to convert a Python list into an array.

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:22.753
Once the values are stored as an array, we can use NumPy operations directly.

00:00:22.753 --> 00:00:29.773
For example, we can add, subtract, multiply, or divide all values in one statement.

00:00:29.773 --> 00:00:36.478
When you run the example, look carefully at the output and compare it with a normal Python list.

00:00:36.478 --> 00:00:43.186
The values may look similar, but the array now supports a much richer set of numerical operations.
